                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "238854276",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197998827138",
                            "num_reviews": 568,
                            "playtime_forever": 713,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 181,
                            "playtime_at_review": 713,
                            "last_played": 1792989652
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is so close to being a great game, but the power creep over the years clearly made the new player experience very, very unfun.\n\nQuests have multiple difficulties: Casual, Normal, Hard and Elite. That's great! I love when MMORPGs have difficulty options, like LOTRO from the same devs does!\n\nThe problem: you can't play Hard or Elite on your first try. You need to play Normal, and then Hard, and then Elite. \n\nNormal and Hard is like a mobile auto-play game where everything dies in one hit and never deal any damage to you.\n\nIt seems like enemies in Normal / Hard mode have been designed close to the power level of an actual 3.5 D&D monster of that level. But the player has MASSIVE bonus over what a normal dnd character would have. You'll have over large AC bonus and attack bonus right from the start, and stuff an extra +4d6 fire damage on every hit on a level 2 character, etc.\n\nAnd since you have to play every quest three times if you want to play Elite, which is the only fun mode, you'll overlevel and then back to the problem of everything being too easy again.\n\nBuying the VIP subscription allows instant access to Hard and Elite while you're subscribed. I don't mind spending money in this game - my account is Premium already, I don't mind paying for content like adventure packs and expansion packs - but the VIP pricing is hard to justify. It's BRL 75 here, while, for example, wow is BRL 50 and FFXIV is BRL 30.\n\nI'd be very willing to play more of it and change this review if they ever change this system or, at least, make Normal dungeons a bit less of a bad joke.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1793298839,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1793299671,
